---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE, ATTRIBUTION } from "../lib/site.mjs";
---

<Base
  title="About & independence"
  description="Who publishes the Australian Election Tracker, how it is funded, its independence statement, legal authorisation and contact details."
>
  <div class="wrap wrap-narrow section">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Independent by construction</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The Australian Election Tracker is an independent public-interest project published by
      {SITE.publisher}. Its purpose is narrow and deliberate: record who is standing, where,
      and what evidence supports each claim — then publish the whole thing as open data.
    </p>

    <h2 id="independence">Independence statement</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The tracker is not affiliated with, funded by, or directed by any political party,
        candidate, campaign, lobby group or electoral commission.
      </li>
      <li>
        It receives no payment from any party or candidate, and no party or candidate has
        any right of review over its contents before publication.
      </li>
      <li>
        Should the project ever carry sponsorship or advertising, it will be non-political,
        clearly disclosed on this page, and structurally incapable of affecting candidate
        ordering, coverage or verification.
      </li>
      <li>
        Editorial decisions follow the <a href="/methodology">published methodology</a>. The
        rules are written down first and applied to every party the same way.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="verify">Why you don't have to take our word for it</h2>
    <p>
      The dataset is a public Git repository, not a database behind a login. Every record,
      every source, every correction and every editorial rule is a commit with a timestamp
      and an author. You can read the entire history, check any claim against its source,
      and reuse the data yourself.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={SITE.repo}>Read the repository</a>
    </p>

    <h2 id="limits">What this site is not</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Not an electoral commission.</strong> The
        <a href="https://www.vec.vic.gov.au/">Victorian Electoral Commission</a> is the
        authoritative source for enrolment, nominations and results. Where we differ from
        the VEC, the VEC is right.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Not polling or prediction.</strong> No opinion polls, no forecasts, no
        preference recommendations, no candidate ratings.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Not complete.</strong> Verification is progressive and ongoing. Coverage
        gaps reflect what we have verified, not what exists.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="authorisation">Legal authorisation</h2>
    <p>
      Victorian electoral law requires certain electoral matter to carry an authorisation
      statement identifying who is responsible for it. This site publishes factual,
      sourced information about candidates and does not solicit a vote for or against any
      party or candidate.
    </p>
    <p class="auth mono">
      Authorised by Colin Dixon, 2 Fern Court, Mallacoota VIC 3892.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Postal address: PO Box 327, Mallacoota VIC 3892. Enquiries about this authorisation,
      or about the site's compliance obligations, can be sent to the contact address below.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Corrections and additions are best raised in public so the reasoning stays on the
      record: <a href={SITE.issues}>open an issue</a> with a source. For anything else —
      including matters concerning a named individual that you would prefer not to raise
      publicly — write to
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Requests for correction concerning living people are prioritised over all other work.
    </p>

    <h2 id="licence">Reuse</h2>
    <p>
      The election data is published under
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" rel="license">CC BY 4.0</a> —
      you may reuse it, including commercially, with attribution to
      <code>{ATTRIBUTION}</code>. The site and tooling code are MIT-licensed. See the
      <a href="/data">open data page</a> for files and citation guidance.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  h2 {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  ul strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .auth {
    padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--surface-2);
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
